---
description: How to author blog posts and MDX custom components
globs: content/**/*.{md,mdx}
alwaysApply: false
---

When creating or editing posts under `content/`, follow [content/guides/content-authoring.mdx](content/guides/content-authoring.mdx).

- Files in `content/` publish. Nested path = slug (`content/math/set/intro.md` → `/blog/math/set/intro`). Learn courses live under `content/learn/` → `/learn/...`.
- Use `.mdx` if the post needs `Figure`, `CodeTabs`, or `PathVisualizer`. Do not import components.
- Shared frontmatter (blog + learn): `title`, `excerpt`, `tags`. Blog also requires `date`; optional `coverImage` + `coverImageAlt`. Learn course roots (`content/learn/<course>/index.mdx`) **must** declare `tags` (hub filters by course-root tags only). Learn-only optional: `icon`, `badge`, `order`. Loader accepts legacy `description` as an alias for `excerpt`.
- Layout already renders the title — start the body at `##`.
- Fenced code auto-renders as `CodeBlock` (card shell + header + dark panel). Use `title="filename"` for a copyable path in the header. Line numbers are on by default; use `hideLineNumbers` to opt out.
- Multi-file = `<CodeTabs>` with editor-style tabs; each fence needs `title="filename"`. Diffs/focus/errors use `[!code ++]` comments, not screenshots.
- Math is `$inline$` / `$$display$$` (KaTeX). Images live in `public/` and are referenced as `/...`.
- Handwritten annotations: `<Mark type="underline|circle|box|highlight|strike-through|bracket" color="warning|#hex">…</Mark>`; optional `note` + `noteLayout` / `noteVariant` / `noteMaxWidth` / `noteColor`. Default ink `#F08F87`. Presets: `default`, `note`, `tip`, `info`, `warning`, `danger`, `success`, `accent` — or any CSS color.
- Never use `MultiFileCodeBlock`, `CodeFrame`, or `DocsCodeBlock` in content. Never put docs or drafts in `content/`.
